################################################################################################
# THREAD 2: COMPLEMENT-EVEN REFRAME of the Node-3 spectrum sum (kind-pasteur kpswf13)
#   e<->N-e (cluster T^op) vs x->-x (circle).  Does the complement-EVEN cluster part
#   determine SPEC?  Plus the frequency-n Z_2 grading of SPEC.
################################################################################################

================================================================================================
(1) CLUSTER REFLECTION INVARIANCE:  cover_set(E) =?= cover_set(N-E) =?= cover_set(-E)
    (if TRUE for all x, then ghat is UNCHANGED by e->N-e: GOOD only sees the cluster
     up to speed-reflection.  Tested EXACTLY on the common breakpoint refinement.)
================================================================================================

  k=8 consec (AP-like, R'~0.73):  E=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]   meas(cover_set(E))=0.327211
    cover_set(-E) == cover_set(E)? False   (the x->-x / speed-negation invariance)
    N=  7: N-E=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]  cover(N-E)==cover(E)? True  meas=0.327211  (meas eq? True)
    N=  7: N-E=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]  cover(N-E)==cover(E)? True  meas=0.327211  (meas eq? True)
    N= 14: N-E=[7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]  cover(N-E)==cover(E)? False  meas=0.276909  (meas eq? False)

  k=8 consec small P (R'~0.63):  E=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]   meas(cover_set(E))=0.327211
