================================================================================================
(2) COMPLEMENT-EVEN SYMMETRIZATION:  SPEC(E) vs SPEC(E u (N-E))  [the conjecture]
    center N = max(E)+min(E).  pairs e<->N-e; fixed: 2e=N; asym: N-e not in E.
    CONJECTURE (HYP-2867): R'/SPEC controlled by the complement-EVEN part; odd cancels.
================================================================================================

  k=8 consec (AP-like, R'~0.73):  P=[1, 2, 3, 12, 13]
    E          = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
    N=7: pairs=[(0, 7), (1, 6), (2, 5), (3, 4)]  fixed=[]  asym(odd)=[]
    E_evensym  = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
    SPEC(E)        = -0.087331   R'(E)        = 0.733058   base=0.327153
    SPEC(E_sym)    = -0.087331   R'(E_sym)    = 0.733058   base=0.327153
    Delta SPEC (sym-E) = +0.000000   Delta R' = +0.000000   [E already even: must be 0]

